[38;5;252m[1m## One real bug found and fixed[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mtranslation/src/lib.rs[0m exported [38;5;10mextern "C" fn driver(c: c_char)[0m. rustc tags an [38;5;10mi8[0m C-ABI parameter [38;5;10msignext[0m, so LLVM assumed the argument register already held a sign-extended [38;5;10mchar[0m, kept the caller's out-of-range value, proved [38;5;10mc ∈ -128..=127[0m, elided the bounds check, and read index 384 of a 384-element table. Calling the export with [38;5;10m256[0m (legal for a promoted C prototype) gave:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mC   : alphabetic: 0     digit: 0     space: 0     printing: 0      to lower: \0
Rust: alphabetic: 1024  digit: 2048  space: 8192  printing: 16384  to lower: \x80
[0m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
gcc's [38;5;10mchar[0m-taking callee reads only the low 8 bits, so C's answer equals the [38;5;10mc == 0[0m answer. Fixed by taking [38;5;10mc_int[0m and truncating ([38;5;10marg as c_char[0m), which is ABI-indistinguishable for real callers, plus masking the table index with [38;5;10m0x1FF[0m so an out-of-bounds read is impossible by construction. [38;5;10mc_src[0m was not modified.[0m[0m
